From c41b449ed9a3db216296de55d098763449501e42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:30:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] refactor(daemon): R8b step 6 the executor consumes
 AgentRuntimePort (required agentRuntime); legacy runtime options, resolvers
 and Codex/Pi option types deleted
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

createAgentExecutor takes `agentRuntime: AgentRuntimePort` in its required object. launch.ts, events.ts, claude/filesystem.ts,
model-receipts.ts and session-coordination.ts import nothing from @jini-ai/agent-runtime any more: definitions, launch resolution,
env, models, filesystem policy, sessions, stream parsers and the startup-failure formatter all come through the port.
Deleted options: runtimeState, getAgentDef, resolveAgentLaunch, ensureAgentCapabilities, applyAgentLaunchEnv, resolveModelForLaunch,
assertClaudeFilesystemSupport, attachAcpSession, attachPiRpcSession, preparePromptFileForAgent, prepareAgentLogFile, codexDisablePlugins,
piGracefulShutdownMs (the Codex/Pi policies and their env precedence live in the bound runtime). Deleted: resolveAgentRuntimeDeps,
resolveCodexDisablePlugins, pi/options.ts, pi/contracts.ts.
§12.8: selectAgentExecutorHostEnv({ env, hostEnvNames }), resolveSystemPromptOverlayDelivery(input, { capabilities }) read when the run
launches (only an explicit false withholds the flag); failRunBeforeStart carries the host's startupMessage with a startup exception.
Hosts: the server preset binds the native runtime (bindAgentRuntime seam, default createAgentRuntimeBindings), minimal-host, reference-web.
Tests: agentRuntimeFixture (the real binding with scripted members) replaces per-option injection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
